Upper bound: CaDiCaL 2.1.2 (in the Lean toolchain) searched and wrote an LRAT certificate; `ZLrat.check_sound`
turns the kernel's acceptance into unsatisfiability. Lower bound: a colouring found by the same solver, checked by
the kernel. Known values (Chvátal 1970; Brown 1974); nothing new is claimed — this is the chain's calibration.
MEASURED 2026-11-06: W(3,5) certificate 130 LRAT lines, ~9 s in the kernel; enumeration would be 2^22 colourings. -/

